# Dependencies
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
yarn.lock

# package-lock.json IS committed. Ignoring it is a library convention — a
# library publishes a version range and must resolve fresh for each consumer.
# leak-lock is an application: nobody installs it as a dependency, so there is
# no reason to leave resolution floating. Committing it pins every transitive
# version and records a sha512 integrity hash per package in the repository,
# which is the only in-repo pin on the bytes that get packaged into the .vsix.

